# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
# NOTE: NO backticks and NO dollar-sign in the desc/blurb text below (shell-eval fragility -- see CLAUDE.md).
register_gate "tests/test_append_falsepause.py" "APPEND FALSEPAUSE GATE: PASS" "append false-pause (the canonical multi-agent pattern is not a hard pause)" "append false-pause: two PRs that EACH APPEND a brand-new independent function to DISJOINT new lines (past EOF-at-base) of the SAME real source file are DEMOTED from a hard serialize/pause (action_required) to a non-blocking heads-up (serialize_soft / neutral) while the collision stays VISIBLE -- recall-safe. The finer engine (_file_pair_symbol_overlap) returns a new relation 'append' when one side appends STRICTLY PAST the file max known symbol end-line (a provable past-EOF additive tail, no graph span) AND the other side is ALSO a past-max append OR a fully-mapped DISJOINT interior edit sharing NO symbol; the verdict ladder softens 'append' exactly like a low-value runner-list overlap, and is_material_coupling is False for serialize_soft so the pause tier never pauses it. Proven against the LIVE engine on a constructed real extractor graph (content-free): append-vs-append (incl. a 118-line gap) and append-vs-disjoint-interior -> serialize_soft + the change is non-material; and the recall controls STAY hard/unchanged -- two edits to the SAME existing symbol -> serialize, two OVERLAPPING edits in one symbol -> serialize, an append that SPILLS INTO an interior edit -> serialize (not past-max -> unknown -> hard), existing DISJOINT symbols -> clear (the pre-existing finer win), and an append-soft wait must NOT mask a real same-symbol collision on the same change -> serialize" "append false-pause fix: append-vs-append (and append-vs-disjoint) on one file -> serialize_soft (neutral, never action_required) but still visible; same-symbol / overlap-into-symbol / append-into-interior stay hard; disjoint-existing stays clear; a soft append never masks a real collision" 24
